AWS Lambda least-privilege IAM policy example:

```json
{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:GetObject"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::my-app-data-bucket/input/*",
      "Condition": {
        "StringEquals": {
          "s3:x-amz-server-side-encryption": "aws:kms"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "dynamodb:PutItem"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:123456789012:table/ProcessResults"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "logs:CreateLogGroup",
        "logs:CreateLogStream",
        "logs:PutLogEvents"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:logs:us-east-1:123456789012:log-group:/aws/lambda/my-process-function"
    },
    {
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": ["s3:*", "dynamodb:*"],
      "Resource": "*",
      "Condition": {
        "Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "false"}
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

**Security principles applied:**
- Specific actions only (GetObject, PutItem — not s3:* or dynamodb:*)
- Specific resources only (exact bucket path, exact table — not *)
- Encryption condition (require KMS for S3 reads)
- Deny non-SSL transport
- Minimal logging permissions

**Azure Functions equivalent:**
```json
{
  "properties": {
    "roleName": "Process Function Role",
    "description": "Least-privilege role for process function",
    "permissions": [{
      "actions": [
        "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/blobServices/containers/read",
        "Microsoft.DocumentDB/databaseAccounts/sqlDatabases/containers/items/create"
      ],
      "notActions": ["*"],
      "dataActions": [
        "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts/blobServices/containers/blobs/read",
        "Microsoft.DocumentDB/databaseAccounts/sqlDatabases/containers/items/create"
      ]
    }]
  }
}
```
